43f-99d1-d0807e509b62":1,"f623bce3-4929-4b46-b9b7-67303e72e348":2,"821465f8-9778-435f-b949-a44d2261b2ae":3,"c90b3b75-63c0-4029-8c06-2de88a45929f":4,"931a4d07-f060-49e0-b41e-885aaecd07ea":5,"ab256f72-6e5e-4a85-a561-668e05110db9":6,"c7ef79f8-05b3-4067-b477-36d1c0903480":7},"lines":{"821465f8-9778-435f-b949-a44d2261b2ae":["Fish to the morning","Wardens","How far to the second stone?","Wheel to the west","We should go back","It’s three hours to the shore. And the light’s coming.","Lock in the chest","There’s a wreck past the key stone. I saw it last night, when the light came. A big hull, lying north of the road. Old. A chest is a box. A hull is a box.","Lock in the chest","Stop","Don’t move.","Why do you want it so much?","The map. It’s not the Guild’s money. You turned that down.","It’ll be over the road by morning","Maybe sooner.","The seventh stone is waiting for you","We have to go","Now. He can’t walk. We’ll carry him in turns. It’ll be slow.","She was nineteen","And the sea didn’t go out again.","Someone did","You did.","The Guild","That’s the Guild’s boats. And that—","That’s a ferry. That’s one of ours.","Will you go out next time?"],"931a4d07-f060-49e0-b41e-885aaecd07ea":["You know, then","Marrow worked it out. I always wondered whether she would."],"937190e0-d6c4-42e3-924f-4f10b2e2544f":["The tide bell","Master, it’s the tide bell.","It’s going","Nine days","Nine days of low water. The road will come up out of the bay, all the way to Old Merrow. Master, no one has charted it. Not properly. Not since—","Just looking","I know","She’s my master.","I can pay","Maybe","It’s not for sale","Four stones we haven’t found","And the song gives us three signs. Fish, wheel, key. And then lock.","The wreck","We can wait in the wreck.","No","That’s not strange at all.","Why didn’t you tell anyone?","Master, if you knew the tables were wrong—","To the tower","To get the real tables. And then to the road.","There are twelve people on the road right now","The Guild’s crew. They think they have three days. They’ll be in Old Merrow tonight, and when the sea comes back, they’ll be cut off at the wheel stone. Every one of them.","You could ring the bell","Now. Ring it, and they’ll know something’s wrong. They’ll turn back.","Seventh day","Maybe sooner. We have to go now.","How many?","Nobody knows the road past here","That’s rather the point.","She never came","She never knew. They told her he was drowned with the others, and she believed them, and she never came back.","Be quiet","Tobiah","Get them to the top of the tower. All of them. Jory too.","She’s here?"],"ab256f72-6e5e-4a85-a561-668e05110db9":["The Guild will send a crew out on the sixth day","Twelve good people, with sledges and ropes. On the ninth day the tide comes back, and by then we will be home with whatever is worth carrying. All we need is the way.","I’m not here to make trouble for you","I’m here to pay you. A hundred crowns for a chart of the road to Old Merrow, delivered by the fifth evening. Two hundred if it’s good.","This could be a forgery","Three","Three of mine. In Old Merrow.","You don’t know the road past here","She’s in the ferry","With your grandmother, Fenn. They are both of them out of their minds. Get down here."],"afbf6e51-6813-443f-99d1-d0807e509b62":["You want to go out there","He was faster than me","He always was. When the water came, he was ahead.","Tell her no"],"c7ef79f8-05b3-4067-b477-36d1c0903480":["Leave me","Take the twins. Go."],"c90b3b75-63c0-4029-8c06-2de88a45929f":["No","She never sends anyone. That is her trouble.","What do you want, child?","Are they?","Count the stones, girl, count them through","That is all of it, I’m afraid. My mother had more verses, but I was a child and only kept the chorus.","Lock in the chest","I always thought that meant a treasure. Every child does.","Seven stones","The seventh is waiting.","I never thought anyone would sing it for the walking again."],"f623bce3-4929-4b46-b9b7-67303e72e348":[]},"ids":104}},"knowled